WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.540
- [Interviewer] All right,
Repeat. It's all yours.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.473
- [Repeat] All right.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:12.863
My mom.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.723
My mom grew up in Louisiana.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.343
And she had two brothers.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.293
And all through our childhood,

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.110
we would hear about hospitality

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.720
and how people in Louisiana were.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.863
They treated you, you
know, and made you welcome.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.453
Welcome to where you'd wanna go back.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.760
My mom used to drink like a fish

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.560
until my father died in '67.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.490
I remember looking up at my mom,

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:53.890
first time I can remember seeing her cry

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:56.180
and 'cause my father was dead.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.630
I didn't know the reason.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:02.630
And from that day on, she
never took another drink.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:03.523
You know?

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.403
Well we, where I grew up,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.373
I had to-

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.880
Well I was always like somebody

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.780
in challenging.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.400
I was challenged in school

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.410
to where I wanted the highest grade.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.013
I wanted the higher score.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.730
I wanted to finish my test first,

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.660
I wanted to get more answers right.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.253
So it was like a competition
thing always with me.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.550
And I would realize that I
wouldn't know anyone competing.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.483
That all of us was competing.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.260
In fourth grade,

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:47.490
we were introduced to Algebra.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.600
And it was so exciting at that age

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.830
because it was something we didn't know.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.100
And the individual mathematician

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.470
who started teaching us
algebra in the fourth grade,

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.415
he would come once a week.

00:02:00.415 --> 00:02:05.415
And he would give us these
problems that were phenomenal.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:10.920
And he wouldn't give us the answer,

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.270
but he would give us the solution.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.263
And we would work solution.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:19.360
All of us would come up
with a. appropriate answer.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.450
But there were other individuals who

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.660
didn't want us to achieve.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.070
So I literally had to
fight to get to school

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:32.360
because, "Oh, you think you smart?"

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.480
Never know I'm not
smarter than anybody else.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.630
I just tried harder.
And I just remembered.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.270
So I had to fight to get to school.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:40.830
And then the same people were
waiting for me after school.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.180
So I had to fight to leave.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.950
So I figured if I had to fight to get in

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:46.932
and fight to get out,

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:51.140
I might as well learn something

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.890
because I'm fighting for it anyway.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:03:00.060
So, in junior high school

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.400
was when my change,

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.120
change in life started.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:13.120
And again, it started when
I started scuba diving.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:18.050
My dive partner, my instructor,
my teacher, my mentor

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.080
was from Bath, Maine.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.700
White guy.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.881
And he'd been to 'Nam.

00:03:24.881 --> 00:03:26.963
And I mean, this guy was-

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.070
To me, he was Einstein.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.920
And I would listen to
the conversation, man.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.530
I'm out of the ghetto

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.380
and I'm ghetto conversation.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.953
But I would hear,

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.860
you know, these affluent people.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.710
I mean, mean heads, bean
heads, call it what you want.

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.310
I would hear them talk.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.760
And I was so amazed at the conversation.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.676
I said-

00:03:49.676 --> 00:03:51.720
(laughs)

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.740
One day, maybe I'll have
conversations like that

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:58.033
So I aspired to increase my vocabulary.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.320
I started aspiring to learn.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:09.740
And with that inspiration,
with every gain,

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.783
every gain brings its own problems.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:13.877
You know, I was always told,

00:04:13.877 --> 00:04:15.660
"You think you're smarter
than everybody else."

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.540
I said, "I'm not smarter.
I just try harder."

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.840
You think you different,
you think you better?

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.780
I'm not better. I'm just different.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.750
You know, I'm just different
from who and what you are

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.050
because I think different.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.173
Anyway.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.460
Anything you consistently do,

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:32.710
you're supposed to get better at.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.800
So I did a lot of fighting.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.100
I did a lot of fighting.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.830
I knew I had to fight, you know?

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:43.190
And anything you keep doing
again, you get better at.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:46.423
So I got somewhat better at it.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.543
When I came out of prison,

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:59.080
I met somebody who changed
my life for a little while.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.420
She was...

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.403
Absolutely a state.

00:05:06.403 --> 00:05:08.240
She was so beautiful to me.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.360
I mean to the rest of the
world too. But she was-

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.810
I would meet her at Pershing Square

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.130
when she come from work
or whatever and meet me.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.820
And I would walk her back in here.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:18.190
I really didn't like her over here

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.400
because she didn't really belong.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.400
But on the way here from
Pershing Square to San Pedro,

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:30.620
I mean individuals would
make the strangest comments,

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.630
like what they wanted
to do to her sexually.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.470
And I would hear this
and I would turn around.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.440
And, "What did you say?"

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.510
And, "Oh, I'm not talking
to you, I'm talking to her."

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:41.180
And one thing I learned
in the military was,

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.650
whoever strikes first and strikes hard

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:47.950
and consistently strikes
has the greatest opportunity

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.310
or possibility of being victorious.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:53.790
So conversation over. I would take off.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:57.220
I would right hook, left, whatever.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:01.940
And there was one particular incident

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:04.370
when this guy came down the street,

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:05.420
he was looking for trouble.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:08.100
He had his shirt off. He
was kinda penitentiary buff.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.030
And I was standing there talking

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:12.110
to the two security guards
in a particular program

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:14.210
where they allow people to
use the bathroom 24 hours.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.770
And so I'm talking to them
and we hear them coming.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.017
So we stopped and we looked and he's like,

00:06:19.017 --> 00:06:20.580
"Yeah, I'm fixin' to fuck me of these."

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:24.090
He used the N word, which I really detest.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:27.060
I mean, in prison, all my years in prison,

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.460
we had a lot of battles over that word.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:32.530
A lot of good people die,
bad people, whatever.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.030
So I particularly tell people,

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:36.960
I mean, I don't care what
your conversation about,

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.060
but when you're talking to me,

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.610
don't use the N word
and don't call me that

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.490
because that's one thing
I aspire not to be.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:45.733
I try hard not to fit that,

00:06:47.008 --> 00:06:48.620
not to wear that jacket.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:53.530
So anyway, he stops in front of me.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:56.080
And then he says, "Yeah, I'm
gonna fuck with somebody up.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.230
Now who's going to be my first victim?"

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:59.480
And he turns around, he looks at me.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:01.220
I'm standing there with the arms folded.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.927
And he says, "You going
to be my first victim."

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:07.020
I said, "Oh, okay, no problem."

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.590
Took my coat off. Put my bag down.

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:09.423
And when it was over,

00:07:09.423 --> 00:07:11.393
he looked different and he felt different.

00:07:12.377 --> 00:07:13.930
And he knew, he knew

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:18.017
because a guy had asked me later, he said,

00:07:18.017 --> 00:07:20.990
"When you hit him and he went
down, what was your thinking?"

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:22.974
I said, "I was thinking I
wasn't gonna let him back up.

00:07:22.974 --> 00:07:23.807
Wasn't gonna give him the opportunity

00:07:23.807 --> 00:07:24.840
to stand back up again."

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.253
Because I kept striking.

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.860
In the particular area I grew up in,

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:35.080
I had no idea that this area

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:38.253
had become a gang.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:44.270
And it was basically like forties.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.040
I had no idea.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.840
I'm in prison and a younger individual

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.670
I knew from that location,

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:55.020
he came and said, "That's what we are."

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:57.330
And I'm trying to think, what is that?

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.927
What is, what does it represent?

00:07:58.927 --> 00:07:59.760
"Oh, we Crips."

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.750
And I said, "Nah, Man.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.450
I mean I'm from there

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.140
by location, not affiliation.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:07.300
I'm not going to do it that way.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.070
I'm gonna keep my particular walk.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.830
I'm not fixin' to get
involved in the gang activity.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.390
I mean, I got your back.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.830
And you know, I have everybody
else's back that I know,

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.600
if and when it comes to it.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.007
But I'm not fixin' to go
into the gang part of it."

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:25.983
One particular day.

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:28.940
And was this?

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.880
I think this was like

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.693
1984.

00:08:35.918 --> 00:08:37.001
End of '84.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.380
I had met this female

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.180
and she wanted to not sexually be involved

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.520
because she was a lesbian,
which is no problem.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:48.483
I'm a lesbian too.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:52.630
She wanted to, you know, take up with me

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.330
and make some money with
me in the ghetto way.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.750
You know, so sell drugs.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:02.140
So I gave her a little something and left.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.250
And I came back about an hour later

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.500
to see how she was doing.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.500
And I went off in the store.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.800
I came out and I looked across the street

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.900
and I noticed, which wasn't
there when I went in,

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.760
there was a crowd.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:15.990
And so I looked at the crowd

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.620
and I seen her in the middle of the crowd.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:18.820
I see her gesticulating.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.590
Moving her head and taking her body.

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:21.867
And I was wondering what was going on.

00:09:21.867 --> 00:09:24.900
And I see this guy I'd never seen before.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:28.560
He walks up to her. He's talking
to her and he pushes her.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.550
And I'm like, what the f-
I'm thinking, what the f-?

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.810
So I crossed the street through traffic

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:37.580
and I walk up and she said,
"Oh, here comes Pete now.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.540
You going to get it."

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.710
And they look at me

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:43.300
and I noticed two girls
I'd never seen before.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:44.800
They back up.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.390
And one goes in the little clutch purse.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.200
And she pulled out a Snap 38.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.460
She handed it to the other one.

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:50.900
She sticks in their pocket.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.940
And you know, they got me covered.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.800
I said, "All right, we're
going to do it this way."

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.570
I said, "I'll be back."

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:58.570
Run down the street.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:09:59.500
Go through a shortcut.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.460
My younger brother's shooting
dice with some friends.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.550
I said, "Come on, man. Let's roll.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:06.340
Call them Hollywood. Let's roll, man.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.327
Motherfuckers drew down on me."

00:10:07.327 --> 00:10:08.160
"They drew down?"

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:10.430
I said, "They drew down
on me, man. Let's go."

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:13.120
We go out to the next
block. Get in the car.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.600
I reach under the
dashboard. Grab the Python.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.280
Open it up. It's loaded.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.113
I tuck it.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:23.910
I say, "Pull around to mom's
house, put it in the driveway."

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:25.690
So we negotiate the turns.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.933
He pulls in the driveway.
I get out of the car.

00:10:27.933 --> 00:10:29.720
I says, "Meet me at the stop sign.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.630
Wait for me right there."

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:34.230
So I march down the middle of the street

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.930
into main trafficking to (indistinct).

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:39.420
And I'm standing there and I'm
looking for the individuals.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:42.200
I don't see them. The guy and two girls.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.400
I catch him on my periphery in a Chevy.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.913
They're about to make a
left turn and come by me.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.690
I act like I don't see them
for another couple of seconds.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:54.280
I reached in and I grab it,
and I go into the stance.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:56.740
And I go into the
stance. They ducked down.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:59.840
But see, I know that the rounds from a 357

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:00.990
is going to go through a car door.

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:02.960
It would go through an engine block.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:06.260
So I sight over the chrome
stripping on the '64 Chevy.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:10.440
And I put two rounds above
the chrome stripping.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.140
And when I dropped the one
under the chrome stripping,

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:14.160
the person pops up.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.050
A female pops up.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:18.163
She'd been hit and
she's flailing her arms.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.960
So the guy grabs her.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.450
He throws her over and he
jumps in the driver's seat.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.780
He's looking up and now like
this, trying to get it in gear.

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.030
And so now I'm thinking I
might as well blow it up.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.480
So I tried to get the gas tank.

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:33.310
I put two rounds in the gas tank.

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:34.700
Don't go up.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.440
And he negotiates the turn.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.660
Clips the car. Pulls down the street.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:40.930
And I take out the back window.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.310
I never understood why
about three blocks down,

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.060
he shoot in the air two times.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:46.920
I guess he was showing, don't pursue me.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.053
We got something too.

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:54.560
So anyway, everybody in traffic, it just-

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.480
everybody jumped out of the cars and ran.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.130
I mean, I would have did the same thing.

00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:01.240
They evacuated the cars
and near down the street.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.810
So I walked back over to my brother's car.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:06.000
We get in and we drive off.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.983
We had approximately,

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:14.760
I would say somewhere around 15 shootouts.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.420
And when I say shootout, I mean, you know

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:20.660
us shooting at somebody else
and they're shooting at us.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.173
And the thing with me is,

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:27.523
when the military trains you on something,

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:32.640
they put a couple of
thousand years of science

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.810
and untold billions of dollars into the,

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:37.450
you know, the training session.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.990
So if you listen,

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:44.610
then the best experts in
the world on how to kill,

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.980
how to make sure the bullet
goes where it's supposed to.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:49.810
Ballistic arching and everything else.

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:53.040
And I just take these
things into consideration,

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.160
especially Kentucky windage.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.030
When you fire, see where
your round is going.

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:59.070
If it's short, lift it.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:03.420
If it's going forward, lower it some.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.720
So I didn't draw down on a lot of people

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.260
because the thing was,
in our neighborhood,

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:10.610
if you draw down, you're going to use it.

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:12.660
The worst thing you can do
is draw down on somebody,

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.730
pull out a pistol, and not use it.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:19.090
Then you fall into another
category where you got a pistol,

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.040
you'll draw down, but you won't use it.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.093
You have to use it.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:28.290
There are a few things

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:31.260
that I've accomplished.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:34.430
And these aren't good things.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:35.263
Things I'm proud of.

00:13:35.263 --> 00:13:37.500
Now that I think about them as an adult,

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.850
I wish I'd never done them.

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:41.820
Can't go back and scrub the past.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:44.710
So living for the future to

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:47.520
probably pass some messes on.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:52.090
If one person get it
and can avoid, you know,

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:55.410
what I've been through or
what I'm still going through,

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.243
then fantastic.

00:13:56.243 --> 00:13:59.270
If nobody can avoid what I went through,

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.160
no one gonna put the message out there.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:04.850
And this medium has turned out to be

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:07.560
one of the best things
that ever happened to me

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:10.690
because there are a lot of

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:14.621
unexpected surprises.

00:14:14.621 --> 00:14:18.210
I ran into a guy I never
knew, but he knew me.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:23.210
He knew me from watching this program.

00:14:23.508 --> 00:14:25.020
And I was amazed.

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:27.560
I still carry that with
me to where, you know,

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:28.880
he wanted my autograph.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:33.540
And I never thought I
achieved anything like that.

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:34.450
But he got to mention this.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.300
He said, "Your story was great.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:37.920
I mean, me and my wife loved it.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:41.140
I mean, you know, you knew
what you were talking about.

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:43.220
It was real. And we loved it.

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:45.820
We told a lot of our friends
and they passed it on."

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:49.330
I shared it with my family.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.290
My son...

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.790
should be getting out of

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:01.640
an incarcerated situation real soon.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.800
I didn't know he was there.

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:07.240
My niece, Rose.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:10.610
She was telling me, "You
need to check on your son.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:13.090
You need to find out
what's going on with him.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:14.820
Something's wrong."

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:16.720
And I really didn't get the message

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:21.590
because I was kind of, well, not too busy.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:25.650
I was preoccupied with my own yo-yo life.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:26.803
The ups and downs.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.910
His mom's been trying to reach out to me

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.930
and I'm not taking that trip again.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:39.010
So I really don't deal with it.

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:41.420
Don't want to, because I will never ever

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.920
go through that cycle again.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.370
It was a bad time in my life.

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:51.683
But nothing compares to what
I recently went through.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.900
The individual I was with,
the female I was with,

00:15:56.900 --> 00:16:00.423
had just, for whatever reason,

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:05.690
told me that she needed some extra money.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:06.903
And a lot of it.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.520
It was critical for me because

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:16.330
it was like she was daring
me to go back to yesterday.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.633
To relive the past.

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:23.070
I'm a type of person I
can look at some things

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:26.963
and I can figure out a way
to achieve an objective.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:32.030
So at this time I did probably...

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:39.075
12 acts in 12 days and...

00:16:39.075 --> 00:16:41.520
(laughs)

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:42.750
gave her what she asked for.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:43.583
A lot of it.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:48.630
And it was for her to

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.740
achieve her escape.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:52.900
One thing she said,

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.770
she always told me that I was too violent.

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:58.760
And for her, she was right because I-

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:03.670
At the drop of the hat,
I take off on somebody.

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:05.300
But I wouldn't go looking for trouble.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:06.590
They'd have to say something,

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:11.390
something derogatory towards
her and disrespectful to me.

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:13.780
So what she did was

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:17.310
she claimed to have lost her house key.

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:18.503
So I gave her mine.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:22.963
Went out today, came back.

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:26.338
Knocking on the door. I couldn't get in.

00:17:26.338 --> 00:17:27.171
I didn't know if anybody was home.

00:17:27.171 --> 00:17:30.913
She was home, but she was
on quiet. Silent running.

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:33.453
So I left.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.760
Went grocery shopping.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:39.400
Came back with a couple
hundred dollars worth of food.

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:41.190
And I'm still trying to get
in. I know she'll pop up.

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:42.940
So I sit there.

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:46.183
A little while later, the police show up.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:49.520
When they show up, the way they come in,

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:52.860
I know, I mean there's no doubt about it.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.370
I know they're coming for me.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:57.720
I just can't figure
out why. What did I do?

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:00.210
So, you know, they draw down.

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:01.980
Lay me down in the hallway, cuff me up,

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:04.210
and take me out to the car.

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:07.200
And say I violated a restraining order.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:08.700
There's no restraining order against me,

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.200
but it was what she told them.

00:18:11.383 --> 00:18:13.540
That she had a restraining
order. She didn't.

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:18.540
However, when they put me
in the car, I gave him,

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.970
I gave him a Bunco. I gave him an alias.

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:26.410
And he typed it in and he said,
"No, let's try this name."

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.563
And when he put my real name in,

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:31.723
there was no doubt in my mind
that she had given it to him.

00:18:31.723 --> 00:18:33.337
That she had set this whole move up

00:18:33.337 --> 00:18:37.640
and I could not understand why.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.230
So, I mean, when something's
too difficult to understand,

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:43.730
I stop trying. I stop
trying to understand.

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:45.530
Either it'll come to me or it won't.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:50.283
But what she did was she got rid of me.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:54.080
She got rid of me so that
she could make her egress.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.660
And she did.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:58.410
I did a little time in Little Beirut,

00:18:58.410 --> 00:18:59.610
what they call the County Jail.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:02.333
Because when you, when
you going to LA County,

00:19:03.289 --> 00:19:04.760
(laughs)

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:06.200
you might not live to get out.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:11.200
And it's a racial riot
just about every day.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:16.220
And I'm a little bit, well a lot older

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:17.980
than I was when I went in as a youngster

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:19.560
looking forward to these activities.

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:20.900
I don't look forward to them

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:23.300
because not everybody
lives to get through them.

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:28.060
The County Jail, they had
their rules and regulations,

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:31.940
but each race has a variety
of rules and regulations

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:35.060
that makes it so much more unbearable.

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.370
So much harder for an
individual to get through.

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.170
So as an older individual,

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:41.050
they usually put us in
the old man's dorm where,

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.810
there's a lot less politics.

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:44.660
Or myself, the veterans' dorm.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.130
So they have me in the veterans' dorm

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:49.830
with watered down politics.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.623
There're still politics,
but they're watered down.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:57.010
I came out of the County Jail

00:19:57.010 --> 00:20:00.350
and I ran into her a couple of times

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:04.650
and just decided to let her go.

00:20:04.650 --> 00:20:08.030
And I have. I think about it,
but I decided to let her go.

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:11.400
However, for a while I was on that...

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.223
I was on that self destruction mode.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:21.810
I was literally really, really trying to

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:24.090
be destroyed.

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:25.707
I didn't want to do it myself.

00:20:25.707 --> 00:20:27.420
Somebody who's going to facilitate me.

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:29.810
Somebody who's going to help me.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:31.880
So I did a lot of things
that I wouldn't normally do.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:35.420
I mean, even when Eva did all those stunts

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:37.030
because he didn't give a fuck.

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:38.713
I didn't give a fuck.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.390
I put myself in a lot of

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:44.120
perilous situations where people-

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:46.453
not the police.

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.760
Oh, I really don't deal with them.

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:50.910
I avoid them at all costs.

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:52.580
But I put myself in the some situations.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:55.390
I mean, I put out a gang of money

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:58.401
and let three guys follow
me into the alley just to

00:20:58.401 --> 00:21:00.370
(laughs)

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:02.173
see how it was going to turn out.

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.170
As it turned out, I came out. They didn't.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:11.183
I don't know where I was psychologically,

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:15.350
but that self destruct.

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:18.570
And then, you know the mind altering,

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:20.213
mood changing substances.

00:21:20.213 --> 00:21:22.370
(laughs)

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:25.910
They were a great help.

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.980
Not on the courage factor,

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:31.330
but on the ability to

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:35.210
stay focused for a while.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:37.770
Because after that, I mean,
it's dead to the world

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:42.293
My...

00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:46.660
There's 11 of us in my family.

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:47.503
There was 11.

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:53.070
Two of my brothers died a
year apart. Both at age 21.

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:53.903
Yeah.

00:21:55.382 --> 00:21:59.830
They went out in

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:03.400
tremendous fashion.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:06.533
And what I mean by that
is, I mean heartbreaking.

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:12.070
That changed my mother's life.

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:15.620
It changed our family
structure. Changed everything.

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:18.730
We used to be tighter than
the skin on a golf ball.

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:21.130
I mean, have you ever
tried to feel a golf ball?

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:24.080
Somewhere along the line, we

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:26.790
well, the older ones,

00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:28.410
gravitated towards their own interests

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:30.003
and this family fell apart.

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:38.350
I really don't communicate with my family.

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:40.700
I mean, a couple of members, you know.

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:42.420
And a few other ones.

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:44.053
Hi and bye. How you doing?

00:22:47.200 --> 00:22:50.859
My younger brother is here with me.

00:22:50.859 --> 00:22:53.323
We don't get along.

00:22:54.780 --> 00:22:56.140
But I love him. He loves me.

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:57.950
I'm not going to let
nothing happen to him.

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:00.570
He's not going to let
nothing happen to me.

00:23:00.570 --> 00:23:01.403
If it does,

00:23:01.403 --> 00:23:04.763
then it's going to be-

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:09.873
It's going to be repercussions.

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:14.560
I just started back.

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:19.560
Well, trying to talk to my daughter.

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:25.493
I can't tell you how that's
going, because I have no idea.

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:28.173
I just take it as it comes.

00:23:29.980 --> 00:23:31.943
I'm not necessarily winning.

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:34.803
I am maintaining the purpose.

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:41.510
And it's just about time

00:23:41.510 --> 00:23:44.200
for me to get up out of here.

00:23:46.950 --> 00:23:50.260
Not because this place is any different

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:51.310
from any other place.

00:23:51.310 --> 00:23:53.640
I mean, you, I mean, you got
a lot of people doing nothing.

00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:55.030
And a lot of drugs and everything else.

00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:57.800
I mean, just concentrated.

00:23:57.800 --> 00:23:59.570
But I can do from here

00:23:59.570 --> 00:24:01.863
the same thing I can
do from anywhere else.

00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:06.570
If I made up my mind to. When I decide to.

00:24:06.570 --> 00:24:09.393
And I've made that decision.

00:24:11.770 --> 00:24:14.730
I'm going to escape Alcatraz,
you know, escape from here.

00:24:14.730 --> 00:24:15.743
I am going to.

00:24:17.440 --> 00:24:21.453
Monday I should be back at work.

00:24:22.950 --> 00:24:24.610
I'm going there. They'll rehire me.

00:24:24.610 --> 00:24:28.120
I mean, I didn't leave
under bad conditions.

00:24:28.120 --> 00:24:30.040
I left under good conditions.

00:24:30.040 --> 00:24:32.290
And I work hard.

00:24:32.290 --> 00:24:34.033
I can, and I will.

00:24:35.500 --> 00:24:36.500
I'm not leaving this

00:24:39.484 --> 00:24:40.930
because I'm scared.

00:24:40.930 --> 00:24:42.693
I'm not leaving because I'm tired.

00:24:44.700 --> 00:24:48.400
I'm leaving it because
there's a graduated process.

00:24:48.400 --> 00:24:51.133
I mean, upward and onward.

00:24:53.190 --> 00:24:57.160
And I'm going to

00:24:59.060 --> 00:25:01.520
show a few other people how.

00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:04.030
I don't know their reasons for being here.

00:25:04.030 --> 00:25:06.850
Their reasons for living.
Their reasons for leaving.

00:25:06.850 --> 00:25:08.743
I mean, I don't know.

00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:11.170
But what I do know

00:25:12.640 --> 00:25:17.393
is I have grandchildren now
that I never physically seen.

00:25:18.390 --> 00:25:19.587
Never spoken to.

00:25:19.587 --> 00:25:23.563
And I been here about, I been
on this side about four years.

00:25:24.950 --> 00:25:27.030
I've never embraced them.

00:25:27.030 --> 00:25:28.200
I've never shaken hands.

00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:30.050
I've never sat down and ate with them.

00:25:30.050 --> 00:25:31.150
I've never taken them anywhere.

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:32.680
I've never presented them anything.

00:25:32.680 --> 00:25:35.163
I've never met them.

00:25:36.396 --> 00:25:38.780
Other than a phone conversation,
a couple of minutes

00:25:38.780 --> 00:25:41.840
because, for me, it's so uncomfortable.

00:25:41.840 --> 00:25:44.080
And it should be. It's supposed to be.

00:25:44.080 --> 00:25:47.000
It's supposed to be uncomfortable

00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:48.883
because I put it off for so long.

00:25:50.920 --> 00:25:55.920
I have six grandchildren

00:25:56.640 --> 00:25:58.190
and I've never met one of them.

00:26:00.910 --> 00:26:05.670
The only person I've actually
seen was my second eldest.

00:26:05.670 --> 00:26:06.503
My son.

00:26:07.410 --> 00:26:08.520
I haven't seen my daughter.

00:26:08.520 --> 00:26:10.343
I haven't seen my youngest.

00:26:12.010 --> 00:26:13.033
But I'm going to.

00:26:16.640 --> 00:26:18.293
There are some things that I-

00:26:19.260 --> 00:26:23.360
Well, I was thinking at one time that

00:26:25.330 --> 00:26:27.470
leaving here, I had to clean up

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:32.030
a few messes that, you
know, I've encountered.

00:26:32.030 --> 00:26:33.003
A few people.

00:26:34.705 --> 00:26:35.630
And I really was.

00:26:35.630 --> 00:26:38.540
I mean, I had it, not mapped out,

00:26:38.540 --> 00:26:40.110
because you don't have to map it out here.

00:26:40.110 --> 00:26:41.073
I'll run into them.

00:26:42.333 --> 00:26:45.433
And I was going to let a
few down. A few of them.

00:26:46.670 --> 00:26:47.910
But I've decided not to.

00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:50.880
I'm not going to. That's not my position.

00:26:50.880 --> 00:26:54.380
That's not. I can't do another 31 years.

00:26:54.380 --> 00:26:56.693
I can't do another 31 days in prison.

00:26:57.810 --> 00:26:58.763
I don't want to.

00:27:00.960 --> 00:27:02.310
I got something else to do.

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:07.600
And I've listened to

00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:09.883
a lot of individual stories on here.

00:27:10.730 --> 00:27:14.230
And I thought I had it hard.

00:27:14.230 --> 00:27:17.043
Everybody had it hard in
their own individual way.

00:27:18.190 --> 00:27:20.950
Because when the strong get
hungry, the weak don't eat.

00:27:20.950 --> 00:27:22.460
I mean, you get fed down here,

00:27:22.460 --> 00:27:27.460
but we talking Darwin's
theory of the fittest.

00:27:27.840 --> 00:27:29.193
You can really see it here.

00:27:31.130 --> 00:27:32.363
No matter who,

00:27:34.070 --> 00:27:37.350
when an individual first
came here, I told him.

00:27:37.350 --> 00:27:40.460
I said, "If you got any
property that you want to keep,

00:27:40.460 --> 00:27:43.470
when you leave, put it on your
back and take it with you."

00:27:43.470 --> 00:27:46.350
He would wonder why I had
three or four backpacks.

00:27:46.350 --> 00:27:47.670
I said, "Because everything in here

00:27:47.670 --> 00:27:50.163
is something I want to maintain.

00:27:51.170 --> 00:27:53.570
And tell me if you don't
want it, just leave it.

00:27:55.070 --> 00:27:56.520
It'll disappear on its own.

00:27:56.520 --> 00:27:58.637
It will go, go to where the dinosaurs."

00:28:05.010 --> 00:28:07.930
I don't want to do any
more fighting down here.

00:28:07.930 --> 00:28:11.223
I mean, I'm not a good runner,
so I'm not going to run.

00:28:12.829 --> 00:28:15.950
But I've tried a different
way to avoid conflict.

00:28:15.950 --> 00:28:17.860
It felt strange. It felt funny.

00:28:17.860 --> 00:28:21.870
It felt like I was, I think
the word is eating crow.

00:28:21.870 --> 00:28:24.040
And I felt kind of, well, not kind of,

00:28:24.040 --> 00:28:28.680
I felt humiliated just by backing down.

00:28:28.680 --> 00:28:31.630
I mean, I had no doubt in my mind

00:28:31.630 --> 00:28:33.103
how it would have turned out.

00:28:34.088 --> 00:28:36.680
It would've looked different
and felt different.

00:28:36.680 --> 00:28:37.920
But I just didn't want to.

00:28:37.920 --> 00:28:39.440
And I wanted to try it another way.

00:28:39.440 --> 00:28:42.193
And I tried it. It didn't
feel good at first.

00:28:43.190 --> 00:28:46.270
But I think in time, it's
supposed to come easier

00:28:46.270 --> 00:28:48.290
to avoid conflict or walk away from it

00:28:48.290 --> 00:28:52.053
instead of going head on into it.

00:28:54.630 --> 00:28:58.103
I'm obviously a lot older.

00:28:59.540 --> 00:29:01.800
I'm not as handsome as
I once thought I was.

00:29:01.800 --> 00:29:04.370
I'm not as quick as I believe to be.

00:29:04.370 --> 00:29:06.930
I'm not as skilled as I want to be.

00:29:08.550 --> 00:29:10.130
Those aren't the reasons why

00:29:10.130 --> 00:29:12.210
I don't want to participate anymore.

00:29:12.210 --> 00:29:14.140
The reason why I don't
want to participate anymore

00:29:14.140 --> 00:29:18.560
is because I'm...

00:29:18.560 --> 00:29:19.910
searching for a new purpose.

00:29:19.910 --> 00:29:20.743
A new direction.

00:29:20.743 --> 00:29:23.620
I can't say that a new
purpose and a new direction

00:29:23.620 --> 00:29:25.230
is going to be better,

00:29:25.230 --> 00:29:27.280
but I can say it's going to be different.

00:29:28.410 --> 00:29:31.710
And it starts with me
making different decisions.

00:29:31.710 --> 00:29:33.363
You know the saying,

00:29:35.270 --> 00:29:39.160
trying to do the same
thing a different way?

00:29:39.160 --> 00:29:40.563
It doesn't work out well.

00:29:42.050 --> 00:29:46.803
To get new results, I
have to try new things.

00:29:47.980 --> 00:29:52.593
And Monday I start on something new.

00:29:56.097 --> 00:29:57.600
I won't make it out of here Monday,

00:29:57.600 --> 00:29:59.010
but I will go to work Monday.

00:29:59.010 --> 00:30:01.330
And that's a great beginning for me.

00:30:01.330 --> 00:30:03.720
Haven't done it in a
while, but I'm going to.

00:30:03.720 --> 00:30:05.760
Most people want to go to SSI.

00:30:05.760 --> 00:30:07.670
I can do that, but I don't want to

00:30:07.670 --> 00:30:10.610
because there's still
some work left in me.

00:30:10.610 --> 00:30:12.713
And I want to go do this time.

00:30:13.610 --> 00:30:15.014
I've made my decision.

00:30:15.014 --> 00:30:16.949
- [Interviewer] Good for you man.

00:30:16.949 --> 00:30:17.782
I'm proud of you.

00:30:17.782 --> 00:30:18.782
- Fantastic.

00:30:20.379 --> 00:30:21.212
- [Interviewer] I'll miss you.

00:30:21.212 --> 00:30:23.040
- No. (laughs)

00:30:23.040 --> 00:30:24.910
If you're here, you will see me

00:30:24.910 --> 00:30:28.400
because I've seen some people
come through and talk about,

00:30:28.400 --> 00:30:30.495
you know, how, Hey, I
used to sleep right here.

00:30:30.495 --> 00:30:31.328
I used to do that.

00:30:31.328 --> 00:30:33.070
And it's just so amazing.

00:30:33.070 --> 00:30:34.430
They bring their family to show them

00:30:34.430 --> 00:30:35.950
where they've been, what they've done.

00:30:35.950 --> 00:30:38.480
And it's one of those success stories.

00:30:38.480 --> 00:30:40.043
And I plan on being one.

00:30:41.040 --> 00:30:41.930
- [Interviewer] Come on back when you do.

00:30:41.930 --> 00:30:44.450
- Fantastic. I will definitely.

00:30:44.450 --> 00:30:45.283
Alright.

00:30:45.283 --> 00:30:46.203
- [Interviewer] Thank you, man.

00:30:46.203 --> 00:30:47.036
- You're welcome.

00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:50.950
Yeah, Monday I go back to...

00:30:51.852 --> 00:30:54.519
(faded talking)

